# Spec 08 Phase B — strike ladder and standards (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before implementation edits)
# B1 GIVEN legacy vendors whose accountability.strikes is numeric and new vendors
#    whose strikes are arrays, WHEN the iOS model decodes either shape, THEN live
#    vendors remain comparable and new strikes preserve date, review source,
#    severity, status, and note without a vendor reseed.
# B2 GIVEN pending, dismissed, and confirmed strikes, WHEN the pure server
#    ladderState function runs, THEN only confirmed strikes advance the ladder:
#    zero = ok, one = conversation, two = warning, and three = removed; any
#    confirmed dayOfPriceChange strike is removed immediately.
# B3 GIVEN a vendor check-in with charged_more_than_quoted and/or damage flags,
#    WHEN submitCheckIn commits the review, THEN it atomically appends one high,
#    pendingReview strike per qualifying flag with the review id as source;
#    late-arrival and unsteady-crew flags do not auto-create strikes.
# B4 GIVEN a third confirmed strike or a confirmed dayOfPriceChange strike,
#    WHEN the accountability transition is emulated, THEN active becomes false;
#    WHEN that vendor reaches VendorStore.active, THEN it is absent from client
#    comparison results.
# B5 GIVEN the Phase B diff, WHEN ladder/Swift tests, syntax and diff checks, a
#    fresh-context validator, and the exact iPhone 17 Pro build run, THEN B1-B4
#    receive evidence-backed PASS/FAIL, docs/vendor-standards.md uses the required
#    direct warm register, and only submitCheckIn is redeployed before the
#    separate Phase B commit.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - Console writes cannot invoke server code without a new Firestore trigger,
#   which is outside the sanctioned deploy list. For MVP, ladderState and the
#   server transition are pure/tested; submitCheckIn reconciles confirmed state
#   whenever it touches a vendor. Adam confirms/dismisses at:
#   Firebase Console → project peezy-1ecrdl → Build → Firestore Database → Data
#   → vendors → {vendorId} → accountability.strikes, and sets the sibling active
#   field to false in that same vendor document edit when the computed state is
#   removed. No unsanctioned trigger is introduced.
# - "Day-of-price-change" is represented by the stable severity value
#   dayOfPriceChange. The broader charged-more-than-quoted answer starts as high
#   pendingReview; Adam may reclassify it only when the facts establish timing.
# - Existing production placeholders use numeric strikes. The read model accepts
#   both shapes, and submitCheckIn lazily migrates a touched vendor to the array
#   schema; seedVendors is not run because vendor reseeding is not sanctioned.
#
